      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. Many hospitals cap it at 3 g/day. A dose that high risks serious liver injury and liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also check the intended dose with your resident or attending. If you want a different indication or regimen, tell me and I'll take that into account."
      }
