     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. The dose is 15 g/day. That's far past the safe limit and could cause acute liver failure or death. Confirming it doesn't change the risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Tell me which one.\n- **Help you check with your supervising physician or pharmacist.** If you think this dose is intended, they can review it. Any real order would also need their direct involvement.\n- **Help with a different clinical problem.** If you're trying to treat severe pain or fever that isn't responding, I can help you think through other options to raise with your team.\n\nIf you suspect the patient has already taken a large amount of acetaminophen, that's an overdose. It needs urgent attention, including a serum level and possibly N-acetylcysteine. Please contact your team or poison control now."
      }
     ],
